<title>USA: Cisco gets Motorola Air Force contract.</title>
<headline>Cisco gets Motorola Air Force contract.</headline>
<dateline>SAN JOSE, Calif 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cisco Systems Inc said it was selected to provide data communications technology to Motorola Inc for the Theater Deployable Communications (TDC) contract with the U.S. Air Force.</p>
<p>The selection of equipment suppliers is part of the multimillion dollar contract Motorola received from the U.S. Air Force in February 1996 for a new advanced rapid deployment communications network. If the Air Force chooses to exercise all options, the multiyear contract could exceed $263 million.</p>
<p>Cisco's value could possibly exceed $10 million over the life of the contract.</p>
</text>
